  apps/apple/Sources/Dashboard/Widgets/AutomationStatusWidget.swift            (views: surface + panel chrome + states + previews)
  apps/apple/Sources/Dashboard/Widgets/AutomationStatusWidgetContent.swift     (compact + full + row views)
  apps/apple/Sources/Dashboard/Widgets/AutomationStatusWidgetModel.swift       (diagnostics + provider seam + @Observable view model)
  apps/apple/Sources/Dashboard/Widgets/AutomationStatusWidgetProjection.swift  (model + decoding + badge/relative/summary + descriptor/registration)
  apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Dashboard/AutomationStatusWidgetTests.swift            (state-machine tests + helpers)
  apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Dashboard/AutomationStatusWidgetLogicTests.swift       (decoding/badge/relative/summary/descriptor/a11y tests)
  apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings                                (P1/S10 catalog: +13 widget.* keys; reuses widget.freshness.*)

All deliverable files keep the `AutomationStatusWidget` prefix (the gate's
check-placeholders -Path prefix and the commit `git add` prefix both match).
Split into 4 source + 2 test files to honor the repo's 400-line/file SwiftLint cap
(largest pre-existing file is 390 lines); decomposition is preferred over a monolith.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARCHITECTURE (ADR-002 / ADR-004 / ADR-009 / ADR-013)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* @Observable AutomationStatusWidgetModel owns LoadableState<[AutomationStatus]>,
  freshness (WidgetFreshnessPolicy fresh/stale/offline), and the optimistic toggle.
  No networking/business logic in the view (P4 binding rule #3): I/O sits behind the
  AutomationStatusProviding seam (P1/S8 state-holder), wired by the composition root.
* States rendered (all 6): loading (skeleton chrome), empty (friendly EmptyState),
  error (TSQueryError + retry), stale (chip + 30s poll), offline (cached + offline
  chip), loaded (compact/full adaptive). Superset of the web (which only branches
  loading/error/empty/data) - the extra stale/offline chips satisfy the prompt's
  required states without dropping any web branch.
* SI/units: N/A (no unit-suffixed fields on this surface).
* Telemetry (P1/S11): WidgetDiagnostics emits `view.opened surface=AutomationStatusWidget`
  exactly once on first appear (os.Logger, redacted, asserted by a unit test).
* Accessibility: VoiceOver labels on every interactive element (refresh button,
  per-row toggle "<Toggle> <name>", combined row label), Dynamic Type (system fonts/
  tokens), reduce-motion (TSFadeIn/TSSkeleton honor it).
* i18n: every string is a LocalizedStringKey resolved through Localizable.xcstrings;
  no English literals in code.
* Registration: AutomationStatusWidget.descriptor (id=automation-status, 2x4/1x2/4x40,
  category=automations) + AutomationStatusWidget.registration(provider:) factory the
  dashboard grid consumes; clamp() enforces the same min/max the web registry declares.

